{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1540 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f2c4a7cf86cf3eeb290c73ab3291d2d09cda63262801c76d1047cd355fc93c71" :edb/db-before-t 1539 :edb/db-after-t 1540 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534852 50 #inst "2026-10-08T09:05:00.998Z" 13194139534852 true] [17592186064009 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139534852 false] [17592186064009 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186064009 1145 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}-1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{0}^{1}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[4-0]-5[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =4-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186064009 1145 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\color{red}-1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x - 1}{x + 1}dx &= ∫_{0}^{1}(4 - \\frac{5}{x + 1})dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}4dx - 5∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x + 1}dx \\\\\n&= 4x\\begin{vmatrix}_{0}^{1} - 5\\ln & x + 1\\end{vmatrix} \\mid _{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= [4 - 0] - 5[\\ln 2 - \\ln 1] \\\\\n&= 4 - 5\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534852 false] [17592186064010 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139534852 false] [17592186064010 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186064010 1145 "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{2x^{2} - 3x - 4}{x - 3}dx &= ∫(2x + 3 + \\frac{5}{x - 3})dx \\\\\n&= x^{2} + 3x + 5\\ln \\mid x - 3 \\mid + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534852 false] [17592186064010 1145 "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division. \n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{ 2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3} .\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+3x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186064011 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139534852 false] [17592186064011 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186064011 1145 "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{x - 1}{2x - 1}dx &= ∫(x - 1)/(2(x - \\frac{1}{2}))dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(x - 1)/((x - \\frac{1}{2}))dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\color{red}\\dfrac12$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 1)/((x - \\frac{1}{2})) &= 1 - ((\\frac{1}{2}))/((x - \\frac{1}{2})) \\\\\n&= 1 - (1)/(2(x - \\frac{1}{2})) \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{1}{2x - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{x - 1}{2x - 1}dx &= \\frac{1}{2}∫(1 - \\frac{1}{2x - 1})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}[x - \\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}2x - 1 & ] + C \\\\ = \\frac{1}{2}x - \\frac{1}{4}\\ln & 2x - 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534852 false] [17592186064011 1145 "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}\\dfrac12$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} & =1-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186064147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314885 13194139534852 true] [17592186064147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314897 13194139534852 true] [17592186064147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314904 13194139534852 true] [17592186064147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314911 13194139534852 true] [17592186064147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314918 13194139534852 true] [17592186064148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314861 13194139534852 true] [17592186064148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314882 13194139534852 true] [17592186064148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314891 13194139534852 true] [17592186064148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314925 13194139534852 true] [17592186064148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314932 13194139534852 true] [17592186064156 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314868 13194139534852 true] [17592186064156 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314875 13194139534852 true] [17592186064156 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314939 13194139534852 true] [17592186064156 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314946 13194139534852 true] [17592186064784 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534852 true] [17592186064784 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186064784 1100 "Evaluate $∫_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x - 1}{2x + 1}dx$." 13194139534852 false] [17592186064784 1145 "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2(x+\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})} & =5-\\frac{(\\frac{7}{2})}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{7}{2(x+\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{7}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(5-\\frac{7}{2x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-7{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5x{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|{|}_{0}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5(2-0)-\\frac{7}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2\\cdot 2+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2\\cdot 0+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[10-\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5] \\\\  & =5-\\frac{7}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186314861 1017 #edb/ref 17592186314862 13194139534852 true] [17592186314861 1089 "q-114879" 13194139534852 true] [17592186314861 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534852 true] [17592186314861 1100 "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186314861 1113 #uuid "203b8faf-aa8f-5bc8-8c68-2ac25460b3aa" 13194139534852 true] [17592186314861 1145 "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 3 & 1 \\\\  & 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}=3x+1+\\frac{2}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3x+1+\\frac{2}{x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534852 true] [17592186314862 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314863 13194139534852 true] [17592186314862 1000 #edb/ref 1759218